# Files that are read by a Linux parser regardless of the machine they were
# cloned onto. `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git for Windows default, so without
# these rules a Windows clone gets CRLF here and the quickstart stops working
# verbatim (AC-20) on the one platform most likely to try it first: Docker's
# Dockerfile parser and `sh -c` both treat a trailing CR as part of the token.
#
# Scoped to the files this change owns rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto`,
# which would renormalise every file in the tree at once.
infra/Dockerfile     text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml   text eol=lf
.dockerignore        text eol=lf
*.sh                 text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml     text eol=lf
